            <ArticleTitle>Optical frequency domain imaging for guidance of optimal stenting in the setting of recanalization of chronic total occlusion.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>367-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present an interesting case illustrating how coronary optical frequency domain imaging (OFDI) examination can be used to guide revascularization of a complex chronic total occlusion (CTO) in a patient presenting to our hospital with a 2-year history of angina, dyspnea, and a positive treadmill test. This case demonstrates the potential clinical role of high-resolution OFDI to optimize coronary stent implantation. OFDI may help to limit the coronary area covered by stents to the true coronary lesion.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
